 "verification": {
  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Tables 1 to 6 parsed from the PDF text layer by word positions (rotated drug headers rebuilt from characters, trend arrows stripped), count tables re-added by row and by column against their printed totals; every value of every extracted table then compared by eye with the rendered page images (full pages at scale 3 and zoomed crops), 2026-09-26. The archived PDF was re-downloaded and matched the census file byte for byte (MD5)."
 },
 "notes": "Half-yearly hospital antibiogram of AIIMS Bhopal, 1st January to 30th June 2023: 3221 isolates as printed. Rows are hospital-wide (spec all, set all): Tables 5 and 6 pool all specimens and all locations (OPD, IPD, ICU and Emergency), each cell giving percent susceptible over the number of isolates tested; drugs printed as -, NR, IR or R are left out. Counts: Tables 1 and 2 (by specimen, all locations) and Tables 3 and 4 (by location, all specimens) are two views of the same isolates, recorded as spec x all and all x setting, with each organism's Total from Table 1 or 2 as the all x all count; IPD is recorded as ward. The Emergency column and the Others specimen column have no key and are not recorded, nor are cells printed as \"-\", so the recorded location or specimen counts add up to less than each organism's total. Tables 7 and 8 (percent susceptible by specimen for all Gram-negative or all Gram-positive isolates pooled) are not organism-specific and were not extracted. Up and down arrows (a change of more than 5 points from the previous half-year) are not values and are ignored. Archived copy used (the live site could not be reached): https://web.archive.org/web/20240715132526id_/https://aiimsbhopal.edu.in/AIIMSFiles/annexuredImage/Antibiogram_AIIMS_BHopal_Jan-June_2023.pdf.",
 "issues": [
  "Second reader 2026-09-26: every cell re-read from the page images (scale 3, zoomed crops by column group) before comparing with the file: all 280 cells with their numbers tested (Table 5: all 206, including the three Typhoidal Salmonella values from the note under the table; Table 6: all 74, above the 40% asked for its layout, including the two rifampicin values from its note), all 20 row n and all 147 counts (Tables 1 to 4). The seeded sample of 70 cells (sample_cells.py) is part of this. 0 transcription errors, nothing corrected: no column shift, and organism, n and specimen or location (OPD, IPD, ICU) correct on every row and count.",
  "Second reader: the 8 cells the validator does not keep are printed as recorded (B. cepacia gentamicin 0 and amikacin 0; B. pseudomallei gentamicin 0; M. morganii minocycline 11.8; P. mirabilis minocycline 0; Providencia minocycline 0; Pseudomonas nitrofurantoin 44.4 of 9; Typhoidal Salmonella cefuroxime 43.8 of 16). Tables 1 to 4 add up by row and by column to their printed totals, so there is no count mismatch; MRSA 117 + MSSA 87 = 204, the S. aureus total of Tables 2 and 4."
 ],
